  "reviewTable": "# Remaining libc/zlib: bounded input-to-native source table\n\nRead-only source review for immutable current6e/a7/system8 image. Exact selected source bytes, source Git blobs, qualified Node content rows and actual shipped dependency rows are in SOURCE-PINS.json. The current fullFS inventory is 3530793c\u2026 /31795 objects; the archive is f9f5c926\u2026 . Raw TypeScript is related by the retained current6e build authority, not falsely described as byte-identical compiled JavaScript. No target, compiler, Node/addon, parser fixture, scanner or network request was executed here.\n\n| Real input / consumer | Source path and native boundary | CVE precondition conclusion / gap |\n|---|---|---|\n| Authenticated engine-admin YAML replacement | resource-yaml.ts:47\u201363 validates YAML kind/name/ns/resourceVersion, writes a random temporary path with numeric permission 0600. Node fs.js default write flag `w` is converted by stringToFlags to O_TRUNC/O_CREAT/O_WRONLY; node_file.cc passes int32 flags to libuv; unix/fs.c:367\u2013393 uses open(2). | The YAML is file content, not a C fopen MODE string. This exact JS filesystem path cannot pass request text as `,ccs=`. kubectl native internals are a separate untraced consumer. |\n| Operator-configured alias JSON file | alias-catalog.ts:9\u201335 stat/regular/size check then createReadStream with fixed options and no request flag/mode selector. | Node fs numeric-open boundary applies. Path control is not MODE control. Only the inspected file-read boundary is covered. |\n| Kubernetes summary response \u2192 fixed native addon | secret-client.ts:301\u2013337 receives bounded Buffer chunks; secret-flat-summary.ts loads a fixed app/native/secret-flat-selector.node path, then flat(chunks,limit,namespace). C scan:341\u2013373 accepts buffers and finite limit, parses in memory through N-API. | No filesystem MODE, gzFile descriptor, formatted gz output or request-selected addon filename in this parser path. This does not clear Node host exports or arbitrary other addons. Actual .node is 8dde4ce6\u2026; existing runtime native checks remain distinct. |\n| HTTP Accept-Encoding \u2192 Next response compression | router-server.js:105\u2013113 installs compression; shipped compiled/compression/index.js selects gzip/deflate then Node zlib.createGzip/createDeflate. Module796 requires zlib; body chunks feed stream.write/end. lib/zlib.js \u2192 binding.Zlib \u2192 node_zlib.cc's memory-buffer deflate/inflate. | Peer can negotiate encoding/control body content, not choose a gzFile/nonblocking FD/formatted-write sequence through this API. No gzFile exclusion is claimed for the whole process. |\n| Next image URL/width/quality and fetched image bytes \u2192 Sharp | image-optimizer.js:567\u2013659 validates URL/scheme/local or remote pattern, width and quality;855\u2013893 passes a Buffer to sharp then toBuffer. sharp/dist/input.cjs:58\u201384 stores Buffer; src/common.cc:75\u201383 extracts pointer+length;476\u2013519 passes new_from_buffer to libvips. | Native image parsing is reachable where images are configured/served. JS supplies no fopen MODE or gzFile operation, but retained libvips binary imports fopen64 and contains bundled zlib-ng. Full libvips/codec implementation and external input-to-native internals are opaque here. Do NOT label them unreachable. |\n| Node ICU and startup-snapshot files | src/node.cc:1063 uses constant rb;1495 constant wb;1536 constant rb. Filename may be operator-controlled by startup configuration. | These three inspected Node src fopen sites do not expose a request-controlled MODE. This is not an audit of all V8/OpenSSL/ICU/dependency callsites. |\n| Privileged local operator shell | Fresh session, DB write role and engineAdmin in permissions.ts; POST cluster/kubectl:13\u201327 accepts bounded command text \u2192 k8s.shellExec \u2192 operator-command.ts:10 bash -c. runtime-capabilities enables operatorShell on Linux unless explicitly disabled. | This intentionally permits native program execution by the trusted operator; process cleanup is not a sandbox. BORTUS_DISABLE_PROVISIONING=true does NOT disable this path. No universal fopen/gzFile exclusion is justified. Qualified read-only runtime may refuse creation of the shell helper; this route was not actually exercised in the existing fixture, so no successful shell execution claim. |\n| Provisioning / remote pod command | deploy/start checks provisioning capability before preparation; Dockerfile sets BORTUS_DISABLE_PROVISIONING=true. Pod exec route sends validated remote kubectl exec -- sh -lc text. | Fixed image provisioning is disabled, not all operator capabilities. Remote pod command execution is a distinct target namespace/image. Neither fact clears local native consumers in other supported deployments. |\n| Prisma engines / SWC / OpenSSL / libvips codecs / libc-using utilities | Existing 89-ELF inspection records libc and selected imports; Prisma query/schema engines and SWC are retained opaque native binaries. Shell commands can select additional shipped utilities. | Exact request/options \u2192 fopen MODE and possible dynamic/static gzFile paths in these consumers are not fully traced. Missing source is a specific evidence gap, not a negative finding. The absence of a DT_NEEDED libz entry does not exclude static/dlopen/Node-export access. |\n| Linked Node zlib exports and addon boundary | Actual Node a7 exports gzwrite/gzprintf/gzvprintf/gzdopen/gzclearerr and bundles zlib; node_shared_zlib=false. Existing inspection found no direct DT_NEEDED system libz consumers among inspected image ELFs. | Exported APIs are genuinely present and could be used by new/opaque native code. The retained gzwrite/gzvprintf/gzclearerr source supports an outstanding-external-input + stalled nonblocking FD + error-clear + later formatted-output hazard; ordinary gzopen does not itself request O_NONBLOCK. No exploit was run, no older-version immunity inferred. |\n| nscd-specific libc DNS